  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/C5D21A">Remark <span data-tag="C5D21A">3.2.5.14</span>.</a> Remark <a href="/tag/CC5FC7" data-tag="CC5FC7">3.2.5.8</a> has an evident analogue for the functors ${\mathfrak F}^{+}$: for any functor $g: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ between small categories, the diagram of left adjoints </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { (\mSet )^{\calD } &amp;  (\mSet )^{\calC } \ar [l]_{g_{!} } \\ (\Set ^{+}_{\Delta })_{/\Nerve (\calD )} \ar [u]_{ {\mathfrak F}^{+}_{\bullet }(\calD )} &amp;  (\Set ^{+}_{\Delta })_{/\calC } \ar [u]_{{\mathfrak F}^{+}_{\bullet }(\calC )} \ar [l] } \]
</div>
  <p> commutes up to canonical isomorphism. </p>
